 <!DOCTYPE html>
 <html lang="en">
 <head>
   <meta charset="UTF-8">
   <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
   <title>Cat FAQ</title>
   <style>
     :root {
       color-scheme: dark;
       --bg: #0b1020;
       --bg-accent: #121a31;
       --panel: rgba(20, 28, 52, 0.9);
       --panel-border: rgba(156, 173, 255, 0.2);
       --text: #eef2ff;
       --muted: #b6c0e0;
       --highlight: #8ab4ff;
       --highlight-strong: #a78bfa;
       --shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
     }

     * {
       box-sizing: border-box;
     }

     body {
       margin: 0;
       min-height: 100vh;
       font-family: Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
       background:
         radial-gradient(circle at top, rgba(138, 180, 255, 0.14), transparent 32%),
         linear-gradient(180deg, #10172d 0%, var(--bg) 50%, #070b16 100%);
       color: var(--text);
     }

     main {
       width: min(860px, calc(100% - 2rem));
       margin: 0 auto;
       padding: 4rem 0 5rem;
     }

     .hero {
       margin-bottom: 2rem;
       text-align: center;
     }

     .eyebrow {
       display: inline-block;
       margin-bottom: 1rem;
       padding: 0.35rem 0.8rem;
       border: 1px solid rgba(138, 180, 255, 0.25);
       border-radius: 999px;
       background: rgba(138, 180, 255, 0.08);
       color: var(--highlight);
       font-size: 0.85rem;
       letter-spacing: 0.08em;
       text-transform: uppercase;
     }

     h1 {
       margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
       font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4rem);
       line-height: 1.05;
     }

     .hero p {
       max-width: 42rem;
       margin: 0 auto;
       color: var(--muted);
       font-size: 1.05rem;
       line-height: 1.7;
     }

     .faq {
       display: grid;
       gap: 1rem;
     }

     .example {
       border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
       border-radius: 20px;
       background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(25, 36, 69, 0.95), rgba(14, 21, 40, 0.92));
       box-shadow: var(--shadow);
       overflow: clip;
       backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
     }

     .question {
       width: 100%;
       display: flex;
       align-items: center;
       justify-content: space-between;
       gap: 1rem;
       padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
       border: 0;
       background: transparent;
       color: inherit;
       text-align: left;
       font: inherit;
       font-size: 1.05rem;
       font-weight: 650;
       cursor: pointer;
     }

     .question:hover,
     .question:focus-visible {
       background: rgba(138, 180, 255, 0.08);
       outline: none;
     }

     .question-text {
       line-height: 1.4;
     }

     .icon {
       flex: none;
       width: 2rem;
       height: 2rem;
       display: grid;
       place-items: center;
       border-radius: 999px;
       background: rgba(138, 180, 255, 0.12);
       color: var(--highlight);
       transition: transform 180ms ease, background-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
     }

     .question[aria-expanded="true"] .icon {
       transform: rotate(45deg);
       background: rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.18);
       color: #d8c8ff;
     }

     .details {
       display: grid;
       grid-template-rows: 0fr;
       transition: grid-template-rows 220ms ease;
       border-top: 1px solid rgba(156, 173, 255, 0.14);
     }

     .details.is-open {
       grid-template-rows: 1fr;
     }

     .details-inner {
       overflow: hidden;
     }

     .details p {
       margin: 0;
       padding: 0 1.4rem 1.35rem;
       color: var(--muted);
       line-height: 1.7;
     }

     @media (max-width: 640px) {
       main {
         width: min(100% - 1rem, 860px);
         padding-top: 2.5rem;
       }

       .question,
       .details p {
         padding-left: 1rem;
         padding-right: 1rem;
       }
     }
   </style>
 </head>
 <body>
   <main>
     <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
       <div class="eyebrow">Cat Care FAQ</div>
       <h1 id="page-title">Common questions about cats, answered clearly.</h1>
       <p>
         Explore quick guidance on behavior, routines, and care for indoor cats. Each answer starts
         collapsed so you can open only what you need.
       </p>
     </section>

     <section class="faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-1">
           <span class="question-text">Why do cats purr?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-1" hidden>
           <div class="details-inner">
             <p>
               Cats often purr when they feel calm and content, but they can also purr when seeking
               comfort, bonding with people, or soothing themselves during stress. The surrounding
               context usually explains what the purr means.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">
           <span class="question-text">How much sleep does a typical cat need?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-2" hidden>
           <div class="details-inner">
             <p>
               Most adult cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day. Kittens and older cats may sleep
               even more, especially if they are growing, conserving energy, or simply enjoying a
               quiet indoor routine.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">
           <span class="question-text">What should indoor cats have for enrichment?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-3" hidden>
           <div class="details-inner">
             <p>
               Indoor cats benefit from scratching posts, climbing spots, window perches, puzzle
               feeders, and regular play sessions. Rotating toys and creating vertical space can help
               keep them mentally engaged and physically active.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">
           <span class="question-text">Why do cats knead blankets or laps?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-4" hidden>
           <div class="details-inner">
             <p>
               Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts in kittenhood during nursing. Adult cats
               often keep the habit because it signals relaxation, familiarity, and a sense of safety
               in a favorite resting spot.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-5">
           <span class="question-text">How often should a litter box be cleaned?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-5" hidden>
           <div class="details-inner">
             <p>
               Scoop at least once a day and change litter fully on a regular schedule based on the
               litter type and number of cats. A clean box supports good bathroom habits and can
               reduce stress-related avoidance.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>
       </div>
     </section>
   </main>

   <script>
     const toggles = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

     toggles.forEach((button) => {
       button.addEventListener("click", () => {
         const details = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
         const isOpen = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

         button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isOpen));
         details.hidden = isOpen;
         details.classList.toggle("is-open", !isOpen);
       });
     });
   </script>
 </body>
 </html>

